You ready to go?

12:22.165 --> 12:23.665
I'll be right with you, dear.

12:23.667 --> 12:25.016
Where are you going?
What about

12:25.018 --> 12:27.702
rubba-dub-dub,
Marty's in the tub?

12:27.704 --> 12:28.670
I'll be right back.

12:28.672 --> 12:30.622
We're just going
to the spa.

12:30.624 --> 12:32.808
Yeah, Marty, you'll be happy.
When I she comes back,

12:32.810 --> 12:34.392
she'll have less hair
than your ears.

12:34.394 --> 12:35.610
But this is date night.

12:35.612 --> 12:37.112
I'll be back by 8:00.

12:37.114 --> 12:40.081
That's after &lt;i>Wheel.&lt;/i>
I'll be asleep.

12:40.083 --> 12:42.400
I'll make it up
to you in the morning.

12:44.871 --> 12:46.538
I'm 91-and-a-half!

12:46.540 --> 12:49.357
I can't plan that far ahead!

12:49.359 --> 12:50.909
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

12:50.911 --> 12:52.294
That was amazing.

12:52.296 --> 12:53.829
It was.

12:53.831 --> 12:55.147
You seen my underwear?

12:55.149 --> 12:56.364
Do you mean...

12:56.366 --> 12:58.550
these?

13:00.303 --> 13:02.370
You know what? Keep 'em.

13:02.372 --> 13:04.472
Ooh, thank you.

13:04.474 --> 13:05.640
Where you going?

13:05.642 --> 13:07.893
What do you mean? Home.
We're done.

13:07.895 --> 13:10.145
So it's just wham, bam,
thank you...

13:10.147 --> 13:12.547
incredibly powerful,
yet sensitive lover man?

13:12.549 --> 13:15.567
Aw, don't get my panties
in a bunch.

13:15.569 --> 13:17.719
I'm serious. We never talk.

13:17.721 --> 13:19.404
Because we're not dating.

13:19.406 --> 13:21.139
I thought you were okay
with this.

13:21.141 --> 13:23.358
I am. That doesn't mean
we can't take an interest

13:23.360 --> 13:24.826
in each others' lives.

13:24.828 --> 13:27.629
For example, did you know
Charlie had a daughter?

13:27.631 --> 13:28.864
Really?
Yeah!

13:28.866 --> 13:30.064
That's great!

13:30.066 --> 13:31.533
You can talk to her.

13:33.035 --> 13:35.570
Fine. Whatever.

13:35.572 --> 13:36.955
Oh, for the love of God!

13:36.957 --> 13:38.306
What do you want from me?

13:38.308 --> 13:40.074
Well, if you must know,

13:40.076 --> 13:41.743
she's coming over for dinner
tomorrow night,

13:41.745 --> 13:44.112
and I just thought that
maybe you'd like to join us.

13:44.114 --> 13:45.780
Dinner? Seriously?

13:45.782 --> 13:47.215
Forget I mentioned it.

13:47.217 --> 13:49.718
Okay, look,
I'll see what I can do.

13:49.720 --> 13:50.268
Really?

13:50.270 --> 13:51.436
I'll try.

13:51.438 --> 13:52.804
Oh, thank you.

13:52.806 --> 13:54.773
You've made me so happy.

13:54.775 --> 13:56.391
Great. See ya.

13:57.827 --> 13:58.894
(sighs)

13:58.896 --> 14:01.646
I should've just bought
a damn vibrator.

14:01.648 --> 14:04.449
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

14:04.451 --> 14:06.484
Here ya go, Marty.

14:06.486 --> 14:07.869
Just the way
you like it--

14:07.871 --> 14:10.038
scotch and Metamucil.

14:11.874 --> 14:14.042
Why aren't we eating?

14:14.044 --> 14:15.610
It's almost 6:00.

14:15.612 --> 14:17.245
Where are we, France?

14:17.247 --> 14:19.664
We're waiting for
Alan's girlfriend.

14:20.549 --> 14:23.218
I thought &lt;i>he&lt;/i> was
Alan's girlfriend?

14:27.807 --> 14:29.391
No. I own the house.

14:29.393 --> 14:32.310
It's actually a funny story.
I was on the beach and I went...

14:32.312 --> 14:34.179
Don't care.

14:35.865 --> 14:37.782
Marty, don't be rude.

14:37.784 --> 14:39.935
I'm sorry. Low blood sugar.

14:39.937 --> 14:42.020
Plus, I really don't care.

14:43.773 --> 14:44.889
Unbelievable.

14:44.891 --> 14:47.125
Lyndsey's
not answering any of my calls

14:47.127 --> 14:48.760
and she hasn't returned
any of my texts.

14:48.762 --> 14:50.178
I told you
you were gonna get hurt.

14:50.180 --> 14:52.530
(mocking): I told you you were
gonna get hurt.

14:52.532 --> 14:54.082
You know what?

14:54.084 --> 14:55.517
I'm gonna go get her.

14:55.519 --> 14:57.118
And don't try to stop me.

14:57.120 --> 14:58.637
Okay. Okay.
Okay.

14:58.639 --> 15:00.171
No problem.

15:00.173 --> 15:04.509
Now that buzzkill is gone...

15:04.511 --> 15:07.161
anyone want to get high?

15:07.163 --> 15:09.547
Roll joint!

15:09.549 --> 15:11.433
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

15:13.669 --> 15:14.953
You think Alan's
gonna mind

15:14.955 --> 15:16.154
that we started
without him?

15:16.156 --> 15:17.138
Who's Alan?

15:17.140 --> 15:18.139
(Berta laughs)

15:18.141 --> 15:20.341
You know...

15:20.343 --> 15:24.312
I think I banged Lucille Ball
in this house.

15:25.347 --> 15:27.816
She was
my second-favorite redhead.

15:27.818 --> 15:30.468
Thank you.
(chuckles)

15:30.470 --> 15:32.287
Wait a second.

15:32.289 --> 15:33.705
It's night.

15:33.707 --> 15:36.241
Why am I still here?

15:36.243 --> 15:38.910
I'll see you tomorrow.

15:38.912 --> 15:40.528
Are you okay to drive?

15:40.530 --> 15:41.680
I'm fine.

15:41.682 --> 15:43.548
Well, let me know
when you get home.

15:44.383 --> 15:46.685
I'm home.

15:46.687 --> 15:48.053
(chuckles)

15:48.055 --> 15:50.055
Your father would've loved
this night.

15:50.057 --> 15:52.524
We're all drunk, we're all high,
and Alan's not here.

15:52.526 --> 15:54.509
Wait-- who's Alan?

15:54.511 --> 15:56.728
You know what
we should do tomorrow?

15:56.730 --> 15:58.430
Go to the Malibu
Police Station.

15:58.432 --> 16:01.016
They took more pictures
of your dad than I did.

16:01.934 --> 16:03.168
Again?

16:03.170 --> 16:06.071
I want to stay home
and play naked &lt;i>Jeopardy.&lt;/i>

16:06.073 --> 16:08.273
I want to spend time
with my daughter.

16:08.275 --> 16:09.274
Granddaughter.

16:09.276 --> 16:11.726
Oh, please,
nobody's buying that.

16:12.862 --> 16:16.397
I am going
into the living room, Evelyn.

16:16.399 --> 16:17.999
I suggest you push me there.

16:18.001 --> 16:20.151
We need to talk.

16:20.153 --> 16:21.503
Be back in a minute.

16:21.505 --> 16:22.771
There's a 50-50 chance

16:22.773 --> 16:24.706
he won't remember
what he wants.

16:24.708 --> 16:26.374
If you're gonna talk about me,

16:26.376 --> 16:29.243
you shouldn't shave
my ears first.

16:31.297 --> 16:32.731
He's great.

16:32.733 --> 16:35.850
Wonder what it's like
to be 91.

16:35.852 --> 16:38.837
I imagine that you're wet in the
places you used to be dry

16:38.839 --> 16:41.406
and dry in the places
you used to be wet.

16:42.691 --> 16:44.659
What's wrong?

16:44.661 --> 16:48.029
Your granddaughter is coming
between us...

16:48.031 --> 16:50.331
and not in the good way.

16:50.333 --> 16:53.935
Look, Marty, she just came
into my life.

16:53.937 --> 16:55.436
And believe it or not,

16:55.438 --> 16:59.724
I wasn't always the best mom
to Charlie or-or the other one.

16:59.726 --> 17:01.993
Jennifer is my second chance.

17:01.995 --> 17:03.795
You got to make a choice.

17:03.797 --> 17:06.164
It's me or the kid.

17:06.166 --> 17:09.968
I love you, Marty, but I have
to pick my granddaughter.

17:09.970 --> 17:14.288
You know, I have $400 million.

17:14.290 --> 17:17.358
I'm not saying it isn't close.

17:17.360 --> 17:19.511
It's over.

17:20.295 --> 17:25.150
(chuckles)
Okay, I'm bluffing.

17:25.152 --> 17:26.651
I really miss you.

17:26.653 --> 17:30.205
I miss you too, money... honey.

17:30.207 --> 17:33.558
Maybe I can
make it up to you.

17:33.560 --> 17:38.430
If you can make it down to me,
you can make it up to me.

17:41.300 --> 17:45.236
Something tells me that
Marty doesn't want me around.

17:45.238 --> 17:48.640
What?! I can't imagine anyone
not wanting you around.

17:48.642 --> 17:50.658
Really? Because
I'm pretty sure

17:50.660 --> 17:52.710
I'm staying at my grandmother's

17:52.712 --> 17:54.479
because you don't want me
around.

17:54.481 --> 17:57.331
No...!

17:57.333 --> 17:58.550
Maybe...

17:58.552 --> 18:00.685
Yes...

18:02.838 --> 18:04.172
I get it.

18:04.174 --> 18:05.824
You already have Alan.

18:05.826 --> 18:07.392
I do.

18:07.394 --> 18:10.411
Hey, do you think I'd look
good in a jumpsuit?

18:10.413 --> 18:12.464
You'd look good in anything.

18:12.466 --> 18:13.681
That's 'cause I'm good-looking.

18:13.683 --> 18:15.183
I pretend like I don't know.

18:15.185 --> 18:16.568
Shh.

18:16.570 --> 18:21.139
Seriously, if you want privacy,
then why do you have a roommate?

18:21.141 --> 18:23.691
Oh, you know, Alan's
way more than a roommate.

18:23.693 --> 18:26.027
He's my best friend.

18:26.029 --> 18:30.748
He was there for me
when I was all alone.

18:31.617 --> 18:33.935
He even took me
into my own house.

18:33.937 --> 18:37.672
You know, him and-and
his stoner son

18:37.674 --> 18:41.643
and his horny mom
and your dead dad.

18:41.645 --> 18:43.661
I mean, they've really
become my family.

18:43.663 --> 18:45.780
Mine, too.

18:45.782 --> 18:50.185
I guess that means you're
becoming part of my family.

18:50.187 --> 18:53.605
Aw...!

18:53.607 --> 18:57.242
I'm the most masculine
person in this house.

18:57.244 --> 18:59.194
(both laughing)

18:59.196 --> 19:00.562
I like you, Jenny.

19:00.564 --> 19:02.947
I like you, Walden.

19:02.949 --> 19:06.417
If you were a chick,
I would totally do you.

19:06.419 --> 19:09.537
Aw! You, too!

19:10.573 --> 19:14.125
Hey, you're welcome
to crash here any time

19:14.127 --> 19:17.629
you need a break
from Evelyn and...

19:17.631 --> 19:20.915
91-and-a-half shades of gray.

19:20.917 --> 19:22.400
Seriously?

19:22.402 --> 19:23.685
Yeah.

19:23.687 --> 19:26.387
You know, I was thinking about
putting in a home gym,

19:26.389 --> 19:28.306
but big deal.

19:28.308 --> 19:30.508
I'd rather have
a Jenny than a gym.

19:30.510 --> 19:32.894
You and me both.

19:32.896 --> 19:34.412
(both laugh)

19:34.414 --> 19:35.663
I get it.

19:35.665 --> 19:39.150
'Cause Jim and gym
are homonyms

19:39.152 --> 19:41.486
and you're a "hamma-sexual""

19:44.840 --> 19:47.325
It's awfully quiet in there.
Did they leave?

19:47.327 --> 19:50.078
I don't know.
Let me go look.

19:53.499 --> 19:55.667
I shouldn't have looked.

19:57.136 --> 19:59.571
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪
(doorbell rings)

19:59.573 --> 20:03.007
No matter what she says,
do not cry.

20:03.009 --> 20:04.592
You're the prize here.

20:05.761 --> 20:07.929
(hushed):
Alan, what are you doing here?

20:07.931 --> 20:09.097
What are &lt;i>you&lt;/i> doing here?
You're supposed

20:09.099 --> 20:10.298
to be at my house
for dinner.

20:10.300 --> 20:11.616
I said I would try.

20:11.618 --> 20:13.318
And I said I wouldn't cry.

20:13.320 --> 20:15.903
And I guess
we're both liars now.

20:15.905 --> 20:18.590
Would you keep it down?
Larry's here.

20:18.592 --> 20:21.192
What? You don't want him
to hear your whore?

20:22.278 --> 20:26.647
'Cause that's all I am
to you-- your whore!

20:26.649 --> 20:29.334
We agreed
this was just about sex.

20:29.336 --> 20:30.685
Well, forgive me
for falling in love.

20:30.687 --> 20:33.221
Alan, if you don't leave
right now,

20:33.223 --> 20:35.823
you're never gonna see
this again.

20:36.825 --> 20:38.009
Call at your convenience.

20:38.011 --> 20:40.128
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:40.130 --> 20:41.495
(sighs)

20:47.649 --> 20:49.083
[]♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪
(doorbell rings)

20:50.185 --> 20:52.070
I'll get that.
It's probably Lyndsey looking

20:52.072 --> 20:54.322
for a little morning wood
to start her fire.

20:54.324 --> 20:55.723
Know what I'm saying?

20:55.725 --> 20:57.442
I know what you're saying,

20:57.444 --> 21:00.678
I just don't know &lt;i>why&lt;/i>
you're saying it.

21:02.031 --> 21:03.364
Uh, hello?

21:03.366 --> 21:04.999
Mackenzie, you lying bitch!

21:05.001 --> 21:06.300
Uh-oh.
Congo, my ass!

21:06.302 --> 21:08.736
Don't run!
You don't want to run!

21:12.574 --> 21:14.525
Yeah, it feels like home again.

